              "file": "track/items/2026-08-21-type-identity-fully-qualified-paths/domain-types.json",
              "line": 362,
              "message": "`domain::CatalogueDocument::new` and `schema_version` change the schema-version API from `u32` to `CatalogueSchemaVersion`, but neither cites `IN-05`, the spec element that requires that value object. In particular, `schema_version` cites only identity/key anchors `IN-01` and `CO-02`, which are unrelated to this signature change.",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "SoT integrity / action incoherent with baseline",
              "file": "track/items/2026-08-21-type-identity-fully-qualified-paths/domain-types.json",
              "line": 687,
              "message": "`domain::CatalogueEntryKey::try_new` is marked `action: modify`, but its declared `try_new(String) -> Result<Self, ValidationError>` signature is identical to the frozen rustdoc baseline. The new `PartialOrd`/`Ord` implementations are separate trait-impl additions and do not make this method a modification; classify the method as `reference` unless its public signature actually changes.",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "DRY / duplicated structural declaration",
              "file": "track/items/2026-08-21-type-identity-fully-qualified-paths/infrastructure-types.json",
              "line": 30,
              "message": "`domain::NewTypeGraphCodecError` and `infrastructure::CatalogueToExtendedCrateCodecError` declare the same three variants, equivalent payloads, no methods, and the same failure semantics, while retaining a conversion between them. The catalogues document no layer-specific invariant or information that distinguishes the infrastructure error, so this duplicates the error contract across neighbouring layers.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
